# From the tests of the first compiler: src/sema.rs, `constants`.
==== 1
---- file a.azl (no newline at end)
const A = B
const B = A
fn main() {

}
---- run check a.azl
---- exit 1
---- stdout (empty)
---- stderr
error[E0702]: constant `A` is defined in terms of itself
 --> a.azl:1:7
  |
1 | const A = B
  |       ^
---- asserted 1:7 constant `A` is defined in terms of itself
---- run check --json a.azl
---- exit 1
---- stdout
{"severity":"error","code":"E0702","message":"constant `A` is defined in terms of itself","file":"a.azl","line":1,"column":7,"end_line":1,"end_column":8,"source":"const A = B","rule":"Constants may refer to each other in any order, but not in a circle."}
{"summary":{"errors":1,"files":1}}
